# XSH freelocale()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The function returns nothing and has no errors, so the checks are errno
# (which the text says is left alone for a valid object) and that other objects
# stay usable. Using a freed object is undefined and is never done.

assertion  XSH.freelocale.001
anchor     functions/freelocale.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       freelocale() leaves errno as it was (0 and EDOM are tried) for an
           object returned by newlocale() with base (locale_t)0, for one
           returned by duplocale(), and for one returned by newlocale() with
           a base object.
test       t/001-errno-kept.c

assertion  XSH.freelocale.002
anchor     functions/freelocale.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       Freeing an object does not disturb another one: after freeing the
           first of two independently made objects (and, in a second round,
           the second), the other still gives the POSIX values of the day,
           month, format, numeric and messages items and the POSIX code set.
test       t/002-others-intact.c
